      "width": 587,
      "height": 731,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Noah Bohland",
      "description": "Built in 1931, it was for 3 decades the tallest building built west of the Mississippi River, it is an iconic part of Kansas City's skyline and is the ideal display of art deco style architecture with it's intricate details and extravagant interior. For decades it was the headquarters of KCP&amp;L (now Evergy) which was and has been the primary electric company in the KCMO metropolitan area. They since have moved their HQ to the nearby One Kansas City Place; but the Power and Light building was renovated into luxury apartments and illuminates different colors every night and special colors for holidays such as Halloween and Christmas.",
      "dateCreated": "2020-03-06",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "kansas-city-power-and-light-building-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9yuw",
      "smallPath": "_m/9/y/u/w/kansas-city-power-and-light-building-wp/power-and-light-building-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "PowerandLightBuilding.jpg",
      "title": "File:PowerandLightBuilding.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/PowerandLightBuilding.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PowerandLightBuilding.jpg",
      "width": 1087,
      "height": 1354,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Hello2020121212",
      "description": "The Power &amp; Light Building viewed from the south at night (2020), the historic building built in the 1930s and was the tallest skyscraper west of the Mississippi River until the '60s have been converted into luxury apartments and has lights that illuminate unique colors that coordinate with special events in the city such as sports teams games, holidays, etc.",
      "dateCreated": "2020-09-10",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "kansas-city-power-and-light-building-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9yuw",
