      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Hello2020121212",
      "description": "Art-Deco influenced along with many other Kansas City skyscrapers built in the 1930s and 1940s, the Power &amp; Light Building was an impressive feat of architecture at the time and was the tallest building west of the Mississippi River in the USA until the Space Needle in Seattle was constructed in the 1960s. Today, the P&amp;L Building are luxury apartments.",
